每 20 分钟监测地球上的每一个点，识别出像这个房间一样大的野火，等等。
every point on Earth, every 20 minutes, identifying wildfire at the size of this room, and so forth.

471
00:46:14,720 --> 00:46:21,260
现在，当我思考所有这些危机韧性任务时，我在想我们的目标是什么，我们要走向何方？
Now, when I think about all these crisis resilience tasks, when I think about what is our objective, where are we heading?

472
00:46:21,260 --> 00:46:23,120
这个“北极星”目标非常简单。
The North Star is very simple.

473
00:46:23,740 --> 00:46:27,560
任何人都永远不应该被突如其来的自然灾害惊到。
Nobody should ever be surprised by a natural disaster coming their way.

474
00:46:28,270 --> 00:46:30,280
所以，这正是我们试图解决的问题。
So, that's actually what we're trying to solve for.

475
00:46:30,638 --> 00:46:34,040
我们如何利用预测来让人们做好准备？
How can we use prediction so that people can be prepared?

476
00:46:34,542 --> 00:46:41,180
这样他们既能保护好自己和财产，也能采取相应的行动。
So that both to keep themselves safe, as well as their property, as well as take actions.

477
00:46:41,838 --> 00:46:44,740
所以，我认为这就是我们要走向的方向。
So, I think that's where we're trying to be heading.

478
00:46:44,740 --> 00:47:00,620
当然，要提出正确的问题，这些技术必须能够让你
对世界、洪水、天气、风暴、高温等问题进行提问。
Now, these all technologies are, obviously, in order to have the right kind of questions here,
you need to be able to ask questions about the world, about floods, about weather, about storms, about heat, and so forth.

479
00:47:01,582 --> 00:47:08,836
在某个阶段，我们也意识到，其实我们真正想要的是实现“行星智能”。
At some point, we also observed that, you know what, in fact, what we really want is to have planetary intelligence.

480
00:47:08,880 --> 00:47:17,020
如果我们把所有这些地理空间模型结合起来，引入卫星图像，并构建额外的卫星模型。
So, what if we take all these geospatial models and we're bringing,
you know, satellite imagery, we build additional models of satellites.

481
00:47:17,486 --> 00:47:18,320
我们引入数据。
we bring data.

482
00:47:18,960 --> 00:47:31,060
我们引入一个名为“人口动态”的模型，这本质上是一个关于人群流动的基础模型，
在新冠疫情分析等过程中非常重要。
we bring a model that we developed called population dynamics, which essentially is a foundation model about people's movements that
